WEBVTT

1
00:21:28.194 --> 00:21:34.194
Verse 35 to 39 says, who or what will be able to separate us from the love of Christ?

2
00:21:34.194 --> 00:21:40.194
Difficulties, problems, persecution, lack of food, lack of clothing, danger or death.

3
00:21:40.194 --> 00:21:43.194
It is as it is written in the books.

4
00:21:43.194 --> 00:21:46.194
Because we believe in you, we are in danger of death all day long.

5
00:21:46.194 --> 00:21:49.194
People treat us like sheep that are to be slaughtered,

6
00:21:49.194 --> 00:21:53.194
but in all difficulties we are more than conquerors.

7
00:21:53.194 --> 00:21:55.194
Thanks to him who loves us.

8
00:21:55.194 --> 00:22:00.194
For I am convinced that neither death nor life, neither angels nor demonic spirits,

9
00:22:00.194 --> 00:22:03.194
neither any power, neither things present nor things to come,

10
00:22:03.194 --> 00:22:05.194
neither height nor depth,

11
00:22:05.194 --> 00:22:09.194
no, nothing on this earth will be able to separate us from the love of God.

12
00:22:09.194 --> 00:22:13.194
That love has been given to us by Jesus Christ, our Lord.

13
00:22:19.194 --> 00:22:22.194
Thank you, Joël. Shall we sit down?

14
00:22:25.194 --> 00:22:40.194
How is it, how is it that you sing on a day like this,

15
00:22:40.194 --> 00:22:43.194
I will sing of the goodness of God.

16
00:22:43.194 --> 00:22:50.194
How is it that you sing, all my life you have been faithful.

17
00:22:50.194 --> 00:22:56.194
How is it that you say, your goodness is running after me.

18
00:22:56.194 --> 00:23:01.194
You know, you are here in the church of Jesus.

19
00:23:01.194 --> 00:23:04.194
And we Christians are stubborn.

20
00:23:04.194 --> 00:23:11.194
Very stubborn when it comes to the hope we have in Jesus Christ.

21
00:23:11.194 --> 00:23:17.194
And you just heard a Bible verse from Romans chapter 8.

22
00:23:17.194 --> 00:23:21.194
And you just heard from Bethel about the revelations.

23
00:23:21.194 --> 00:23:30.194
And these are verses that relate to hope and faith and a peace

24
00:23:30.194 --> 00:23:34.194
that cannot be removed by whatever happens.

25
00:23:37.194 --> 00:23:41.194
God continuously tests our faith.

26
00:23:41.194 --> 00:23:45.194
Our faith is continuously tested.

27
00:23:47.194 --> 00:23:51.194
The Bible says that God does not tempt us.

28
00:23:51.194 --> 00:23:53.194
That is a difference.

29
00:23:53.194 --> 00:23:55.194
God does not entice us.

30
00:23:55.194 --> 00:24:03.194
He will never put us in situations where He tempts us to turn away from Him.

31
00:24:03.194 --> 00:24:05.194
There is a difference in that.

32
00:24:05.194 --> 00:24:09.194
But our faith is indeed continuously tested.

33
00:24:09.194 --> 00:24:12.194
In everything we experience.

34
00:24:12.194 --> 00:24:20.194
In the Bible, for example, you see a story where God brings the people of Israel to the promised land.

35
00:24:20.194 --> 00:24:24.194
And then God says to the people of Israel,

36
00:24:24.194 --> 00:24:30.194
Make sure that when you are in the land where it is good,

37
00:24:30.194 --> 00:24:32.194
where there is blessing,

38
00:24:32.194 --> 00:24:34.194
where there is protection,

39
00:24:34.194 --> 00:24:37.194
where the purpose is very easy to see.

40
00:24:37.194 --> 00:24:39.194
Ah, this is God.

41
00:24:39.194 --> 00:24:41.194
God has brought me to a blessing.

42
00:24:41.194 --> 00:24:43.194
Oh, then it is easy.

43
00:24:43.194 --> 00:24:45.194
Then it is easy to recognize God in that.

44
00:24:45.194 --> 00:24:47.194
When it is good.

45
00:24:47.194 --> 00:24:51.194
When you see that God fulfills his promises.

46
00:24:51.194 --> 00:24:53.194
When God keeps his promises.

47
00:24:53.194 --> 00:24:55.194
Then it is easy to see.

48
00:24:55.194 --> 00:24:57.194
Oh, this is God. Yes, of course.

49
00:24:57.194 --> 00:25:00.194
Then I will certainly not forget him.

50
00:25:00.194 --> 00:25:04.194
But even then God says to the people of Israel.

51
00:25:04.194 --> 00:25:06.194
But when you are in the promised land.

52
00:25:06.194 --> 00:25:08.194
When everything goes well.

53
00:25:08.194 --> 00:25:11.194
When all promises are fulfilled.

54
00:25:11.194 --> 00:25:13.194
When you are safe.

55
00:25:13.194 --> 00:25:15.194
When you pursue your ambitions.

56
00:25:15.194 --> 00:25:17.194
Then God says, do not forget me.

57
00:25:17.194 --> 00:25:22.194
For it is precisely when things go well that your faith is tested.

58
00:25:22.194 --> 00:25:27.194
And in the same way, it is also true in the form of sorrow.

59
00:25:27.194 --> 00:25:32.194
It is precisely in sorrow that we are tested in our faith.

60
00:25:33.194 --> 00:25:39.194
Precisely when things are difficult to explain rationally in our minds.

61
00:25:39.194 --> 00:25:41.194
Why God?

62
00:25:41.194 --> 00:25:45.194
Why is this happening to me?

63
00:25:45.194 --> 00:25:50.194
If you are a good God, could you not have prevented something?

64
00:25:50.194 --> 00:25:55.194
If you are a good God, why do you not intervene when I pray?

65
00:25:55.194 --> 00:26:00.194
If you are a good God, why is there still death?

66
00:26:00.194 --> 00:26:05.194
And it is precisely then that your faith is tested.

67
00:26:05.194 --> 00:26:10.194
Not tested in such a way that you are tempted to walk away from God.

68
00:26:10.194 --> 00:26:15.194
But it is precisely then that your faith matters.

69
00:26:15.194 --> 00:26:26.194
But you know, in the last few months, when baby Shiloh was still in mama Maureen's womb.

70
00:26:27.194 --> 00:26:35.194
Even then there were reports that said, from the medical help we have so much respect for,

71
00:26:35.194 --> 00:26:39.194
it was said, this is not going well.

72
00:26:39.194 --> 00:26:47.194
Even then I heard from the parents that God is a God of hope.

73
00:26:47.194 --> 00:26:50.194
That God is a God of purposes.

74
00:26:50.194 --> 00:26:57.194
That God has plans that we sometimes cannot rationally explain.

75
00:26:57.194 --> 00:27:02.194
Then you can see that the faith of the parents was so rock solid,

76
00:27:02.194 --> 00:27:07.194
that it was a testimony to the people in the hospital of Genk.

77
00:27:07.194 --> 00:27:12.194
Praise the Lord, for the faith of this family.

78
00:27:12.194 --> 00:27:17.194
And when baby Shiloh was finally born, it was like,

79
00:27:17.194 --> 00:27:22.194
okay, she is born, but she probably won't make it through today.

80
00:27:22.194 --> 00:27:24.194
Her birth was a miracle.

81
00:27:24.194 --> 00:27:26.194
Her first day was a miracle.

82
00:27:26.194 --> 00:27:29.194
Her second day was a miracle.

83
00:27:29.194 --> 00:27:35.194
And from the first day, what a miracle it was, she survived the first day.

84
00:27:35.194 --> 00:27:40.194
And she could eventually go from the mother straight to the intensive care unit.

85
00:27:40.194 --> 00:27:44.194
And from the intensive care unit, after a few days,

86
00:27:44.194 --> 00:27:49.194
after 48 hours it was said, she is still alive, what a miracle.

87
00:27:49.194 --> 00:27:53.194
And from the intensive care unit, she was allowed to go to daddy and mommy in the regular room.

88
00:27:53.194 --> 00:27:55.194
And that was a miracle.

89
00:27:55.194 --> 00:28:01.194
And there was talk, in the hospital there was talk about the faith of this family.

90
00:28:01.194 --> 00:28:06.194
And eventually, from the hospital, baby Shiloh was allowed to go home.

91
00:28:06.194 --> 00:28:12.194
And so every day, dear church, every day that baby Shiloh has lived,

92
00:28:12.194 --> 00:28:16.194
has been a miracle and a blessing.

93
00:28:16.194 --> 00:28:24.194
I repeat, every day that baby Shiloh has lived was a blessing for this family.

94
00:28:26.194 --> 00:28:32.194
And that is why we can still say, and this is the stubbornness of a Christian,

95
00:28:32.194 --> 00:28:36.194
we are not to be shaken.

96
00:28:36.194 --> 00:28:38.194
Whatever happens to us.

97
00:28:38.194 --> 00:28:46.194
This is not about justifying, but this is about identifying yourself with who God is.

98
00:28:46.194 --> 00:28:52.194
And this is what you need. You need it in all situations of life.

99
00:28:52.194 --> 00:28:56.194
Both in the easy days and in the difficult days.

100
00:28:56.194 --> 00:29:02.194
You need to know God so that you can be a person of hope.

101
00:29:04.194 --> 00:29:11.194
In the Bible, what we just heard from Joel, in the Bible we read from Romans chapter 8,

102
00:29:11.194 --> 00:29:19.194
actually what Paul does is a sort of explanation of why there is still pain.

103
00:29:20.194 --> 00:29:22.194
And I hear this so often from people.

104
00:29:22.194 --> 00:29:26.194
And as I look around the room, I cannot define whether you know God,

105
00:29:26.194 --> 00:29:29.194
or whether you do not believe in God, or whether you might not know,

106
00:29:29.194 --> 00:29:32.194
or perhaps you have a rock-solid trust in God.

107
00:29:32.194 --> 00:29:35.194
Here, the people who are sitting at the front really have a trust in King Jesus.

108
00:29:35.194 --> 00:29:39.194
But as I look around the room, I do not know everyone of course.

109
00:29:39.194 --> 00:29:43.194
And very often I hear from people who do not believe in God,

110
00:29:43.194 --> 00:29:49.194
that they say, if there is a God, why does He not do anything about it?

111
00:29:50.194 --> 00:29:56.194
Unfortunately, as a pastor of a church, I have encountered this situation more often.

112
00:29:56.194 --> 00:30:02.194
And then the question came to me, Tim, and now? How should we explain this?

113
00:30:02.194 --> 00:30:05.194
And then the best explanation we can draw from Scripture,

114
00:30:05.194 --> 00:30:09.194
indeed what Paul wrote 2000 years ago.

115
00:30:09.194 --> 00:30:13.194
Romans eight is actually just an answer in itself,

116
00:30:13.194 --> 00:30:15.194
for the people who know the Bible.

117
00:30:15.194 --> 00:30:19.194
Actually, we all know, the Christians who are here in the room,

118
00:30:19.194 --> 00:30:24.194
when you talk about, how Lord, why then, why then pain,

119
00:30:24.194 --> 00:30:28.194
why still loss, why the loss of a loved one,

120
00:30:28.194 --> 00:30:33.194
why, how should I place this at a moment when I just cannot say, why?

121
00:30:33.194 --> 00:30:35.194
Romans chapter eight.

122
00:30:36.194 --> 00:30:40.194
And we often do in the church, what Joël just did, was perfect.

123
00:30:40.194 --> 00:30:43.194
You take a verse out, and you look at it,

124
00:30:43.194 --> 00:30:46.194
and you declare it as a statement about your life.

125
00:30:46.194 --> 00:30:48.194
This is who we are.

126
00:30:48.194 --> 00:30:53.194
Whatever happens, in times of hunger, in times of joy,

127
00:30:53.194 --> 00:30:58.194
in times of attack, and even in times when we experience death together,

128
00:30:58.194 --> 00:31:01.194
I love Jesus.

129
00:31:02.194 --> 00:31:06.194
I will once, I have always been a real fan of that,

130
00:31:06.194 --> 00:31:11.194
I always enjoy it when we read a Bible verse,

131
00:31:11.194 --> 00:31:14.194
then I always like to look at the context.

132
00:31:14.194 --> 00:31:19.194
Because you can take a verse out, and that verse is powerful,

133
00:31:19.194 --> 00:31:22.194
and it has potential on its own,

134
00:31:22.194 --> 00:31:25.194
and it is a double-edged sword, every verse we say,

135
00:31:25.194 --> 00:31:28.194
but it is also always good to zoom out for a moment,

136
00:31:28.194 --> 00:31:30.194
and then you look at the whole chapter.

137
00:31:30.194 --> 00:31:32.194
What is Paul actually talking about?

138
00:31:32.194 --> 00:31:36.194
So let me take a few Bible verses from Romans chapter 8,

139
00:31:36.194 --> 00:31:42.194
and then I will take you along with what Romans chapter 8 actually has to tell.

140
00:31:42.194 --> 00:31:45.194
Romans chapter 8 verse 1 for example.

141
00:31:45.194 --> 00:31:50.194
But if you belong to Jesus Christ, you are no longer condemned,

142
00:31:50.194 --> 00:31:53.194
for you live in the way that the Spirit wants,

143
00:31:53.194 --> 00:31:57.194
and no longer in the way that your self wants.

144
00:31:58.194 --> 00:32:01.194
And Paul is actually talking about the law here,

145
00:32:01.194 --> 00:32:04.194
that you have been acquitted from that law,

146
00:32:04.194 --> 00:32:07.194
that you no longer have to live in your own way,

147
00:32:07.194 --> 00:32:09.194
or that you have to strive for something,

148
00:32:09.194 --> 00:32:13.194
but you now live in a way that you live to know God,

149
00:32:13.194 --> 00:32:16.194
to live by the Holy Spirit.

150
00:32:16.194 --> 00:32:22.194
But what is stated here, I see in you Randolph, and I see in you Maureen,

151
00:32:22.194 --> 00:32:28.194
I see that you place this situation in the Spirit,

152
00:32:28.194 --> 00:32:31.194
because you are no longer positioned from,

153
00:32:31.194 --> 00:32:35.194
I cannot reconcile this, and therefore I am angry.

154
00:32:35.194 --> 00:32:40.194
I cannot reconcile this, and therefore I walk away from Jesus.

155
00:32:40.194 --> 00:32:44.194
We do not do that, because we know Jesus.

156
00:32:44.194 --> 00:32:48.194
For we do not live by our rational thinking,

157
00:32:48.194 --> 00:32:53.194
we do not live by our opinion, but we live by who Jesus is.

158
00:32:53.194 --> 00:32:55.194
Amen?

159
00:33:19.194 --> 00:33:22.194
And if that same Spirit dwells in you,

160
00:33:22.194 --> 00:33:28.194
He will also give life to your mortal body.

161
00:33:28.194 --> 00:33:32.194
Do you know how much hope this gives for the people in this room?

162
00:33:32.194 --> 00:33:36.194
Do you know how much hope this gives for the people sitting here at the front?

163
00:33:36.194 --> 00:33:39.194
That we may read that we have hope?

164
00:33:39.194 --> 00:33:43.194
There will come a moment when this family will stand face to face

165
00:33:43.194 --> 00:33:46.194
with baby Shiloh, who has grown up in heaven,

166
00:33:46.194 --> 00:33:48.194
for we have that hope from Scripture.

167
00:33:48.194 --> 00:33:51.194
Can I get an amen from all the Christians?

168
00:33:51.194 --> 00:33:53.194
This is the hope we have.

169
00:33:53.194 --> 00:33:58.194
And it hurts now, and it feels distant,

170
00:33:58.194 --> 00:34:01.194
that you say, no, but I want to hold them close to me now,

171
00:34:01.194 --> 00:34:03.194
but this is the hope we have.

172
00:34:03.194 --> 00:34:09.194
There will come a moment when you will ultimately see them standing before God's throne.

173
00:34:09.194 --> 00:34:13.194
Whole, healthy, powerful,

174
00:34:13.194 --> 00:34:19.194
in the ministry and the purpose for which she was born.

175
00:34:19.194 --> 00:34:23.194
For she was born with a purpose, Randolph.

176
00:34:23.194 --> 00:34:29.194
A question within us would be, why Lord?

177
00:34:29.194 --> 00:34:33.194
And I heard this from Maureen in the hospital.

178
00:34:33.194 --> 00:34:38.194
She literally said, I believe to a doctor,

179
00:34:38.194 --> 00:34:41.194
she was born with a purpose.

180
00:34:41.194 --> 00:34:44.194
And the Lord may say it.

181
00:34:44.194 --> 00:34:47.194
Wow.

182
00:34:47.194 --> 00:34:49.194
If you can make such a statement,

183
00:34:49.194 --> 00:34:54.194
that He has control over life.

184
00:34:54.194 --> 00:34:57.194
How long, how short.

185
00:34:57.194 --> 00:35:00.194
How much joy, how much suffering.

186
00:35:00.194 --> 00:35:04.194
How many victories, how many deep valleys.

187
00:35:04.194 --> 00:35:07.194
He is good in every situation.

188
00:35:08.194 --> 00:35:11.194
Verse 14.

189
00:35:11.194 --> 00:35:16.194
Everyone who is led by God's Spirit is a child of God.

190
00:35:16.194 --> 00:35:21.194
For you did not receive a spirit that makes you a fearful slave.

191
00:35:21.194 --> 00:35:23.194
But you received God's Spirit.

192
00:35:23.194 --> 00:35:26.194
He makes you children of God.

193
00:35:26.194 --> 00:35:31.194
Through God's Spirit we call Him with full trust, dear Father.

194
00:35:31.194 --> 00:35:36.194
I wanted to pull this text out to present to us.

195
00:35:36.194 --> 00:35:41.194
How can you say today that God is a dear Father?

196
00:35:41.194 --> 00:35:44.194
Isn't it much better to be angry at God?

197
00:35:44.194 --> 00:35:48.194
Isn't it much easier to say there is no God?

198
00:35:48.194 --> 00:35:51.194
Isn't it much easier to say there is no God?

199
00:35:51.194 --> 00:35:54.194
For I see war and I see hunger.

200
00:35:54.194 --> 00:35:56.194
And I see this and I see that.

201
00:35:56.194 --> 00:35:58.194
And I see death and I see the loss of a loved one.

202
00:35:58.194 --> 00:36:00.194
There is no God.

203
00:36:00.194 --> 00:36:02.194
Do you think that is the solution?

204
00:36:02.194 --> 00:36:06.194
Would that be the solution to our questions?

205
00:36:06.194 --> 00:36:10.194
Is that then the answer there is no God?

206
00:36:10.194 --> 00:36:11.194
No.

207
00:36:11.194 --> 00:36:16.194
It is precisely an answer that you can say I am in Jesus Christ.

208
00:36:16.194 --> 00:36:20.194
Found in the hope that I have a living God.

209
00:36:20.194 --> 00:36:22.194
And that he knows what he is doing.

210
00:36:22.194 --> 00:36:25.194
We do not build our trust on our own self.

211
00:36:25.194 --> 00:36:27.194
For that makes us fearful slaves.

212
00:36:27.194 --> 00:36:28.194
But on him.

213
00:36:28.194 --> 00:36:30.194
He is the resurrection in life.

214
00:36:30.194 --> 00:36:31.194
Amen.

215
00:36:33.194 --> 00:36:37.194
And then here as the last verse 22.

216
00:36:37.194 --> 00:36:42.194
We know that the whole earth is groaning and sighing in pain at this moment.

217
00:36:42.194 --> 00:36:45.194
Until the time comes that God restores everything.

218
00:36:45.194 --> 00:36:47.194
And not only the earth but also ourselves.

219
00:36:47.194 --> 00:36:49.194
We see mourning today.

220
00:36:49.194 --> 00:36:51.194
We see pain today.

221
00:36:51.194 --> 00:36:53.194
We will not downplay it either.

222
00:36:53.194 --> 00:36:55.194
And Christians should not say oh who cares.

223
00:36:55.194 --> 00:36:57.194
Of course.

224
00:36:57.194 --> 00:37:03.194
You know church, we are made in the likeness of who God is.

225
00:37:03.194 --> 00:37:08.194
In other words, we are like God is.

226
00:37:08.194 --> 00:37:13.194
In other words, if God laughs, we have the capacity to laugh.

227
00:37:13.194 --> 00:37:17.194
If God is happy, we have the capacity to be happy.

228
00:37:17.194 --> 00:37:20.194
But the Bible also says, and Jesus wept.

229
00:37:20.194 --> 00:37:24.194
If God weeps, we have the capacity to weep.

230
00:37:24.194 --> 00:37:27.194
Today is a day of tears.

231
00:37:27.194 --> 00:37:32.194
And in the midst of tears, we can say Jesus is here.

232
00:37:32.194 --> 00:37:35.194
I will continue with verse 23.

233
00:37:35.194 --> 00:37:38.194
And not only the earth but also we ourselves.

234
00:37:38.194 --> 00:37:44.194
It is true that we have already received God's Spirit as a foretaste of the heavenly things that we are yet to receive.

235
00:37:44.194 --> 00:37:48.194
But still we groan and sigh now in pain.

236
00:37:48.194 --> 00:37:52.194
While we wait for the moment when God will completely free us.

237
00:37:52.194 --> 00:37:55.194
Then He will make us His children forever.

238
00:37:55.194 --> 00:38:01.194
That will be at the moment when we will be freed from our mortal body.

239
00:38:03.194 --> 00:38:07.194
Maybe we can stand for a moment at the end of my Word.

240
00:38:09.194 --> 00:38:13.194
I do not want to ask this of you if you do not yet know God.

241
00:38:13.194 --> 00:38:18.194
But what Joël just read is the end of my Romans chapter 8.

242
00:38:18.194 --> 00:38:26.194
And I think that all Christians in the room, if you have the faith that Randolph and Maureen and the children have.

243
00:38:26.194 --> 00:38:31.194
Perhaps we can read these Bible verses that Joël just read.

244
00:38:31.194 --> 00:38:33.194
The climax of chapter 8.

245
